{
  "id": "gierer-meinhardt-well-mixed-biology",
  "name": "Gierer-Meinhardt well-mixed activator-inhibitor core",
  "description": "Homogeneous reaction core only: no diffusion, tissue geometry or spatial pattern formation is simulated. Local autocatalysis with inhibitor-dependent suppression differs from repressor Hill feedback. Reconstructs a retired flowless concept. Illustrative normalized source/degradation coefficients(1,1,1,2), initial(1.2,1), horizon30. They give positive stable equilibrium(2,2). No claim these values are a fitted Hydra experiment or the full original spatial model. Signed net-rate flows encode equations, not material transfer claims. No clamps or hidden state resets.",
  "source": "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234",
  "reference": "Gierer and Meinhardt (1972), A theory of biological pattern formation, Kybernetik12:30-39.",
  "category": "biology",
